{"id": "EUVD-2026-81843", "enisaUuid": "63a555c7-b70c-3859-8db1-2e875f48b4ac", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf, cgroup: Fix storage null-ptr-deref after replacing prog\n\nSyzkaller reported a storage null-ptr-deref issue after replacing prog.\nThis occurs in the following scenario:\n1. prog A, an empty prog, is attached to a cgrp.\n2. prog B uses BPF_MAP_TYPE_PERCPU_CGROUP_STORAGE and calls the\n   bpf_get_local_storage helper.\n3. link_update is called to replace prog A with prog B.\n\nThe reason is that __cgroup_bpf_replace fails to alloc and assign the\nrequired cgrp storage for the incoming replacement prog. Consequently,\nthe new prog inherits an uninit storage, leading to null-ptr-deref panic\nwhen kick the new prog.\n\nFix this by rejecting a link update if new_prog's cgroup storage is\nincompatible with link->prog.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:07:51", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:50:38", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/16c8321ee40c420f8e02e09515a5126682ddf4ea", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a033c950f6731be88a7da98604ed78f302f15b80", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1ab3da12061d7ccb099f7e925fa2d865967a316a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/12feca126831556dc7fabe5a3ba28fbd328768b6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3f562c537e9ecf4bc5e206cfffc2cc047f1b7e94"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-90250", "GHSA-364x-ffh5-8mmx"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "014bc774-6398-3a8f-a479-6ef5d1b90504", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0c991ebc8c69d29b7fc44db17075c5aa5253e2ab <a033c950f6731be88a7da98604ed78f302f15b80"}, {"id": "2cd1670e-1746-38b5-8909-117af0ae9be7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0c991ebc8c69d29b7fc44db17075c5aa5253e2ab <16c8321ee40c420f8e02e09515a5126682ddf4ea"}, {"id": "2ddb8554-7672-33ce-b808-24b157e369be", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "2e10033c-44e1-351e-a5d0-82c1d9f4addb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.7"}, {"id": "3a491c39-9b2b-3ad1-9c04-067e3ac26dbd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "7bfa2c30-fe75-3ede-be3e-75a561579f93", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "7c9ff7b3-00db-3f3a-8ad4-c7247545be26", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "82593204-d3e9-3704-a694-b4b393cf4f77", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "88ec808c-880e-3344-bafb-db1471d888fc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0c991ebc8c69d29b7fc44db17075c5aa5253e2ab <3f562c537e9ecf4bc5e206cfffc2cc047f1b7e94"}, {"id": "96ee631c-3328-32d2-8c4a-0c193fcd4edb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "dca38dce-107a-3d2f-8d0f-143f63c30865", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0c991ebc8c69d29b7fc44db17075c5aa5253e2ab <1ab3da12061d7ccb099f7e925fa2d865967a316a"}, {"id": "f33d654c-e8f5-3928-9af6-86dd6558e541", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0c991ebc8c69d29b7fc44db17075c5aa5253e2ab <12feca126831556dc7fabe5a3ba28fbd328768b6"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "4dfe2fa2-9739-3b25-a220-9134ec126b44", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}